VoxLens — third-party components and their terms
================================================

VoxLens's own code and documentation are licensed under the PolyForm
Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (see LICENSE). Nothing in that licence grants rights
in anything listed below. Each carries its own terms, and several are more
restrictive than VoxLens's licence.

Nothing listed here is committed to this repository — no model weights, no
corpus data, no vendored upstream source. They are fetched at setup time or
supplied by you.


Why VoxLens is noncommercial
----------------------------

Not a preference — the only honest option. The licence restriction is inherited,
and it is inherited three times over:

    the recogniser        USR 2.0, CC BY-NC 4.0, covering code AND weights
    our patches           contain excerpts of that code
    the training data     LRS3, TED-derived, CC BY-NC-ND

Relicensing VoxLens's own code permissively would change nothing about that
chain: no commercially-usable visual speech recognition checkpoint was found to
exist at all. A permissive licence here would advertise a freedom the pipeline
cannot deliver, which on a public repository is a claim someone might act on
before discovering it is false.

See docs/adr/0003-usr2-large-non-commercial.md for the full reasoning, and
docs/research/pretrained-checkpoints.md for the survey it rests on.


The recogniser
--------------

USR 2.0 — https://github.com/ahaliassos/usr2
    CC BY-NC 4.0, covering both the code and the released weights.
    Copyright (c) 2026 Alexandros Haliassos.

    Fetched at a pinned revision by scripts/vendor.py into vendor/, which is
    generated and not committed. The files in patches/ are diffs against that
    source and therefore contain short excerpts of it.

    The weights are NOT distributed with VoxLens and are never downloaded
    automatically. You obtain them yourself, under their terms.

    Note that the underlying training data (LRS3, TED-derived) is CC BY-NC-ND,
    which is why no commercially-usable visual speech recognition checkpoint
    was found to exist. See docs/research/pretrained-checkpoints.md.


Runtime dependencies
--------------------

MediaPipe — https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe
    Apache License 2.0. Used for face and landmark detection. The bundled
    face_landmarker.task model carries Google's own model terms.

PyTorch, torchvision, torchaudio — https://pytorch.org
    BSD-3-Clause.

OpenCV (opencv-python) — https://opencv.org
    Apache License 2.0.

PyTorch Lightning, Hydra, OmegaConf, NumPy, tqdm, sentencepiece, PyAV
    Apache-2.0 or BSD-style; see each project for its terms.


Evaluation corpora
------------------

Not distributed with VoxLens, and not committed. Obtained by you, under their
own terms, which are more restrictive than this project's licence.

LRS3 (via the MuAViC re-host)
    TED-derived, CC BY-NC-ND. Withdrawn from its original distribution points.
    Evaluation use only.

WildVSR — https://github.com/YasserdahouML/VSR_test_set
    No licence text is published. The repository has no LICENSE file and the
    README states no terms. Treat as unlicensed: fine for private local
    evaluation, not a basis for redistribution.

Excerpts
    docs/demo.html and docs/demo.pdf quote a small number of short transcript
    lines from the LRS3 test split, for the purpose of illustrating and
    criticising the system's output.


If you are considering commercial use
-------------------------------------

VoxLens's own licence forbids it, and relicensing that alone would not be
enough: the recogniser, its weights, and the data lineage behind them each
prohibit commercial use independently. See docs/adr/0003-usr2-large-non-commercial.md
for the full chain.
